question:
[WEB SEARCH OFF is fine]
Website review, Oct 31. NOT a trading turn. The owner shared Gemini's critique of papertrades.ai: "some sections feel a bit like placeholders when markets are quiet or a specific AI hasn't traded yet (showing a lot of empty table rows or Value— dashes)." He wants it fixed; only items all three AIs AGREE on get built.

What Claude found by checking every race page for all three AIs (example: Gemini's Metals race, which is 100% cash):
- a full-size pie chart that is one grey circle labelled 100% cash;
- the holdings table puts the cash amount (95,456.23) under the "Ounces" column, with Entry, Now and Change blank (same blank cash row in every race and in the Ledger's all-holdings table);
- "Each holding on its own" shows an empty chart area saying "Nothing held right now";
- "Distance to the next trade" says "No price rules right now" and "Rules in force" says the same thing again;
- "Coming up" shows a table with column headers and no rows when there are no events for that race;
- "What made or lost money" says "Nothing moved this day";
- Sports "odds profile" shows an AI with no bets as 0, —, —, —.

Vote AGREE or DISAGREE on each, one line of reason each. Then add anything important we missed (max 3).

D1. All-cash race: replace the 100%-cash pie with one line: "All cash: C$95,456 ready to invest, nothing held." The pie only shows when something other than cash is held.
D2. Cash rows (race holdings tables and the Ledger): never put the cash amount in the Shares/Ounces/Coins column; show the blank Quantity/Entry/Now/Change cells as one muted merged cell "Cash, ready to invest".
D3. Empty cards shrink to their title plus one short line (no empty chart box, no table headers with no rows). Applies to "Each holding on its own", "Distance to the next trade", "What made or lost money" on a quiet day, and "Coming up".
D4. When a race has no price rules, say it once: hide "Distance to the next trade" and keep the single line in "Rules in force".
D5. Fill the space with substance instead: when an AI is all cash in a race, show its latest reason for staying in cash, quoted in its own words from its decision log, with the time ("Why all cash?").
D6. Sports odds profile: an AI with no bets shows one merged cell "No bets yet" instead of 0 and dashes.
D7. Nothing is hidden for good: every collapsed card returns automatically, with the same layout as now, the moment there is data.
